Why MIT-0, and what it covers.

This repository is a kernel: you copy it, run BOOTSTRAP.md, and end up with a wiki
of your own. Attribution is deliberately not required, because the one thing a
template must not do is put a legal to-do in front of every copy.

It covers everything here with no distinction between "code" and "content": the
tools and launchers, the contract and the prompts, the page templates, and the
skeleton itself. Pages you write into your copy are yours, under whatever terms
you choose; nothing in this file reaches them.

The one thing a licence cannot grant is trustworthiness. The citation discipline
in AGENTS.md is a mechanism, not a guarantee: it makes a fabricated citation
detectable by a human, and it is only worth what your own raw sources are worth.
